      "attribute": "keep_location",
      "value": "inner_pocket_of_shirt",
      "quote": "He folded the locket into a pocket of plain cloth and held it to the hollow of his shirt as if it might find room there."
    },
    {
      "entity": "char-thomas-byrd",
      "attribute": "sleeps_with_rose_locket_beside",
      "value": "true",
      "quote": "Thomas crossed the yard and, as he did each night, felt the weight of the locket like a pulse at his chest."
    },
    {
      "entity": "char-mistress-anne-fletcher",
      "attribute": "noticed_missing_apron",
      "value": "true",
      "quote": "\"Mistress, my apron is gone,\" she said. \"I left it by the drain and it's no longer there.\""
    },
    {
      "entity": "loc-kitchen-cellars",
      "attribute": "crate_lining_smell",
      "value": "sun_and_yeast_crate_smell",
      "quote": "In the cellar the crates waited in rows, smelling of sun and yeast."
    },
    {
      "entity": "char-mistress-anne-fletcher",
      "attribute": "found_scrap_of_paper",
      "value": "true",
      "quote": "She read enough to see the curl of a particular letter and the urgency of a short instruction, and folded the scrap into her palm as one folds a small thing that might become evidence or consolation."
    },
    {
      "entity": "char-mistress-anne-fletcher",
      "attribute": "has_not_reported_to_lord_harrow_yet",
      "value": "true",
      "quote": "She did not yet raise the matter to Lord Harrow—there was time for patterns to prove themselves - but she set a weight to the evening now in place of the house's ordinary hum."
    }
  ],
  "presentEntities": [
